Why Hawk-Eye & Why Growth Sports? ❓

This exciting opportunity to join our passionate and enthusiastic team will take you to elite-level sporting events all around the world. As a member of our team, you will be responsible for delivering Hawk-Eye technology across a diverse range of current sports, including Athletics, Gaelic Sports, Volleyball, Horse Racing and Motorsports. Presently, Badminton makes up the large majority of our global deployments, but our landscape can shift quickly. The 'Growth' in Growth Sports is literal: we are a highly agile department built for rapid expansion, significant pivots, and the continuous pursuit of new sporting opportunities. You will play a crucial role in maintaining excellence in our current sports, while helping us deliver innovative solutions to an ever-expanding roster of new clients.  The Growth Sports department delivers our Tracking and Replay products across a wide range of sporting applications, both in the UK and globally. We are always growing and developing new cutting-edge services for our clients, and with this expansion comes the need for new faces to join our team and help drive our ongoing innovation.  Successful applicants will receive training on the basic skills and knowledge required to be a Hawk-Eye operator - and then it’s time to get to an event and get immediately hands-on with our technology! We pride ourselves on supporting the development of our people, and we look forward to challenging you in a job that is truly unique.  ﻿﻿

What Does A Typical Day Look Like? 🛠

Pre-Match & Tournament Preparations: Liaise with key stakeholders such as broadcast personnel, match officials, and teams while taking ownership of our system on-site and representing our company in the best possible manner to ensure all contractual obligations are seamlessly delivered;

Technology Setup: Set up our cutting-edge Tracking and SMART Replay technologies at venues around the world (this can involve physically demanding work, such as rigging cameras and running cables);

System Checks: Conduct thorough pre-match system checks to ensure everything runs efficiently;

Match-Day Operations: Monitoring and operating Hawk-Eye technologies during matches;

Performance Monitoring: Keep a close eye on hardware and software, troubleshooting any issues that arise;

Agile Deployment & Cross-Training: Adapt quickly to operational changes across on-site, office-based, and remote environments, applying your technical knowledge to new sports, systems, and teams as the department expands and pivots;

Post-Match Reporting: Complete detailed reports to enhance future operations and client satisfaction;

Off-Seas

Location : UK-based (Hybrid role with work to be completed as required from on-site, the Basingstoke office and/or WFH at various times).

Travel : Extensive domestic and global travel to Cricket-playing nations (travel, accommodation and daily living allowance expenses paid by Hawk-Eye)

Contract : Full-Time, Fixed-Term - 12 Months

Expected Start Date : Monday 28th June 2027

Why Hawk-Eye & Why Cricket?

Join us at Hawk-Eye to be part of an exciting journey through the world of sports events. Our operational teams play a crucial role in delivering high-quality services at major sporting events worldwide.  As a Placement Cricket Systems Operator, you will be part of our team delivering our world-renowned Ball-tracking & Edge-detection (DRS) technology, Match Officials' Technology (MOT) and suite of Broadcast Enhancement technologies at cricket events all around the world. This role provides a genuine opportunity to create a direct impact on the biggest occasions and moments in cricket; this could be operating the technology to correctly call an LBW decision during an England Test match at Lord's, or telling the story of the impactful bowling spell during the Cricket World Cup Final.  Our powerful hardware and software will allow your creativity to flourish, with ideas and innovation being the main tools behind our success. You will get the opportunity to work with passionate, innovative, motivated and intelligent people throughout the company, who will continually try to push your personal development and engage with your desired long-term career path.

